  "prefLabel": "Cub 203.03 Conduct of a Rulemaking Hearing",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Cub 203.03 Conduct of a Rulemaking Hearing.\n\n(a) Rulemaking hearings shall be presided over by the chairperson of the board or the chairperson’s designee.\n\n(b) The presiding person shall:\n\n(1) Establish the speaking order of those who wish to be heard from a speaker's list;\n\n(2) Cause a record to be made;\n\n(3) Limit the amount of time each speaker may speak, as the number of speakers and amount of time necessitates;\n\n(4) Revoke a speaker’s recognition to speak for reasons provided in Cub 203.04(c);\n\n(5) Effect the removal of any person who disrupts the hearing; and\n\n(6) Adjourn the hearing or pursuant to RSA 541-A:11, recess the hearing and reconvene a hearing at a later date if:\n\na. The number of speakers exceeds the allotted time for the hearing; or\n\nb. The capacity of the room does not accommodate the number of persons who wish to attend.\n\nSource. #8570-A, eff 2-18-06; ss by #10005, eff 9-22-11",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/cub100-300.html"
